WEBVTT

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.980
Okay, that's enough.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.650
You've gotten a lot stronger.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.530
What are we gonna do today?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.020
Spar?

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.670
Nope, today's all about this.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.640
What is it?

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.950
Here.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.620
Take a sniff.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.940
Why do you have this?

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.840
I thought we could drink it together.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.580
I made it by putting honey 
in some forest grape juice.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.160
The honey wasn't easy to get, y'know.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.500
Is something wrong?

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.380
Nah, just... come the winter 
solstice, you'll be an adult.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.640
And a man's gotta get used to this stuff.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.020
Won't Mary be mad about this?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.770
Nah, we'll keep it a secret.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.770
It'll be just between us men.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.530
Okay, let's drink.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.950
All right! Here y'go!

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.570
Cheers!

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.370
Whoa, that's good! Delicious!

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.850
And I even get to drink it with you!

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.940
Yeah. It's good.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.180
The Faraway Paladin

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.190
Okay! Time to test your courage!

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.180
My courage?

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.090
We're gonna take a little peek 
at Mary while she's changing.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.270
But won't we get in trouble?

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.410
Say what?!

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.360
The hallway's spinning...

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.350
C'mon, follow me!

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.390
Hey, you okay?

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.150
I'm fine, I'm fine!

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.680
<i>I can erase my presence easily.</i>

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.090
<i>This'll be a piece of cake!</i>

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.370
Wait! You idiot!

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:21.800
Who's there?!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.710
Crap!

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:23.700
Blood!

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.810
What's the meaning of—ugh, you stink!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.170
What did you make Will drink?!

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.600
Oh, this is just...

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.930
Oh, we were just gonna have a 
little peek while you changed.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.230
Wha... Wha... Wha...

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.930
I told him we shouldn't...

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.490
What do you think you're doing, you idiot?!

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.430
<i>My voice has been changing,</i>

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.380
<i>so I knew I was due for 
my first ejaculation...</i>

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.250
<i>But it was inspired by Mary 
changing... Mary changing...</i>

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.940
What're you washing there, Will?

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.810
Hey, is that...

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.390
Don't laugh!

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.660
<i>I really gotta be careful 
not to drink too much.</i>

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.960
<i>Today's the day of my battle with Blood.</i>

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.940
<i>Once this is over,</i>

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.230
<i>I'll probably be leaving 
this temple by spring.</i>

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:25.990
Could you find a way to lose the duel 
in a way that Blood won't notice?

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.300
<i>Okay...</i>

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.170
Will.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.890
I'll help you get changed.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.260
As of tomorrow, you'll be an adult.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:40.760
Have you decided which god 
you'll swear your oath to?

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.420
Well... Yeah, I've got an idea.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.850
I see.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.630
Mary, I'm gonna win today.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.120
Okay.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.610
Where's Gus?

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.940
Hey, Will. Ready to do this?

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.250
Anytime. Let's do it.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.530
Good. Then, let's go over 
things one more time.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.560
No magic, no trying for instant kills.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.350
Otherwise, anything goes.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.450
If anything happens, Mary will 
fix it with her blessing.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.570
The first one to admit defeat or 
become unable to fight loses.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.000
Try your best not to die!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.290
<i>He's like a storm.</i>

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:55.700
<i>If I take just one solid hit, 
I'll be out of the fight!</i>

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.560
Thought you could get in close, didn't ya?

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.300
Ugh, this is infuriating!

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:19.130
<i>It's a challenge to avoid one 
of Blood's strikes perfectly,</i>

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:23.010
<i>but if I receive one with just my 
sword, it'll shatter along with me.</i>

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:27.050
<i>So how do I survive his strike 
and get into the gap between us?</i>

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.990
<i>There's only one answer!</i>

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:32.860
Here it comes!

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.200
<i>Will...</i>

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.250
He's holding my sword between his ribs?!

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.110
That was pretty good.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.530
I concede.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:04.830
Yep. Man, having no muscles 
really is a disadvantage.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:05.790
Blood!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:06.120
Ack!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.670
Don't you "Ack!" me!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.290
You promised you wouldn't 
use that trick again!

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.400
N-Not sure what you're talking about...

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.360
The one where you use your ribs 
to trap an opponent's weapon!

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.840
Yeah, but I don't have 
organs or anything, so...

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.070
What?! He did that when he was alive?!

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.350
Yes, he did! Can you believe it?!

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:26.450
Well, my opponent at the 
time was really quick!

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.600
And it looked like he was 
gonna stab you, so I just...

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.960
You did not "just" anything!

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.400
I can't believe he survived.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.250
Without my blessing, he wouldn't have!

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.590
Look, I did it 'cause I 
trusted your prayer to work!

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:42.900
I was genuinely concerned 
that you had instantly died!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.560
Didn't I ask you to never do that again?!

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.310
<i>Even I know what this is.</i>

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.970
Do you understand what 
"please don't do it again" means?!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.640
<i>This is one of those things even 
a dog wouldn't butt in on.</i>

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:49.810
It means "<i>don't</i> do it again"!

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.200
Will, even if you couldn't beat me,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.870
what you've accomplished is still remarkable.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.760
Even if you couldn't beat me.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.920
You didn't have to say 
it twice for emphasis!

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.670
I'll make sure you lose next time!

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.120
That's the spirit, little Will!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:06.460
Ow.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.430
Don't get carried away!

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:11.540
Both of you need to take this seriously!

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.430
But you know,

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.590
if I had a killer slash or secret technique, 
I could've taught it to you.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.520
You don't?

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:18.680
Nope.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:22.690
The way I fight and the way 
you fight aren't the same.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.560
My goal was never to raise 
you into an imitation of me.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:31.310
So the moves that I rely on 
won't be the same for you.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.430
It's the basics that matter most.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.060
Make sure you can use all the things 
you've learned at any time.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:42.090
Both Mary and I have already taught 
you everything that's important.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:43.030
Okay...

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.710
Dad, Mom.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.230
"Dad," eh?

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.750
Yeah, I guess that's 
pretty much what we are.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.120
That's true.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.330
I can't teach you any secret techniques,

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:59.610
but to mark your new independence, 
I'll give you this.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.590
It's the most powerful of 
all the demonblades I own.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:06.390
What? But I didn't even win...

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.840
I told you, it's to mark 
your new independence.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.490
Go on, try it out.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.870
It's called "Overeater."

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.560
It ranks at the highest 
level of demonblades.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:25.580
It can even cut down one of the gods' 
Echoes, so long as it can reach them.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.580
The Words engraved in it are 
too difficult to understand,

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.330
but I can sum up its effects:

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.710
"If a living being is cut with this blade,

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.500
its wielder recovers life 
force with each cut."

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.190
Huh? Recover life force?

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.330
Yep. In other words,

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:46.380
you can just swing it around without 
thinking and still be the last man standing.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.880
You're a smart kid, so I'm 
sure you understand this,

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.080
but don't use it any more than you have to.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:56.310
It makes its wielder feel a lot stronger,

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.390
but it's not the type of demonblade 
that enhances your spirit.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:01.690
The more you use it, the more 
dependent you'll become,

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:04.040
until you're so weak that 
there's nothing left of you...

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.330
And then I'll go back to the start 
of the life-and-death cycle.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.310
That's probably part of what 
makes it a "demonblade."

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:12.470
Anyway, I've said a lot, 
but I'm sure you'll be fine.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.290
<i>They both have faith that I 
can use this sword properly.</i>

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:26.170
<i>But am I really someone 
worthy of their faith?</i>

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:29.990
Well, if I'm gonna give you a demonblade,

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:32.640
I guess I gotta tell you 
about its history, too.

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:37.160
Along with what you've been 
wanting to know, of course.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.310
<i>He's talking about what I've 
wondered all these years.</i>

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.030
You are a grown-up now, after all.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:50.690
I promised I'd tell you once you grew up.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:54.200
Your mind and body are both 
plenty big enough now.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:00.630
This is the tale of the king among demon 
kings who tried to conquer this continent,

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:04.000
the one known as the High 
King of the Eternals...

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:07.930
the tale of the defeat and death of 
many heroes, as well as our own...

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:14.670
and the tale of why you grew up here.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:19.380
The Undying Bladefiend.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:20.730
The King Among Kings.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.620
The Purest Evil.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.950
The Inexhaustible Darkness.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.520
The Rider of Warstorms.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.190
They are all names for the 
High King of the Eternals.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.500
About 200 years ago,

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.490
the demon kings led a great uprising.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:39.700
An army of countless demons invaded 
our continent of Southmark.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:43.580
All the continents were crawling 
with demon kings, generals...

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:47.250
The kinds of demons you really 
don't wanna see showing up.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:49.000
Demons?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.820
And these swarms of demons offered up 
massive amounts of flesh and blood

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:57.510
in a number of great rituals to 
their deity, the god of dimensions.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:01.100
In response to this, the minions 
of the god of tyranny, Iltreat,

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.210
and those of the god of 
the undead, Stagnate,

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.390
also became active all over the world.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.660
The virtuous gods expended 
a great deal of strength

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:12.210
in a series of battles intense 
enough to change the map.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.830
I know you learned geography from Gus,

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:17.700
but don't think it's the 
same now as it was then.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.050
Because of that,

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.530
even we don't know much about what the 
other continents were like back then.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:26.560
All we know is that the High King 
went on a rampage in Southmark.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.270
He sure has a lot of scary nicknames.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.870
Frankly, they don't even 
come close to the truth.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:34.800
His abilities were absolutely insane.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.700
He could turn any blood 
he shed into soldiers,

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:42.150
and any flesh cut from his body into 
commanders, in unlimited amounts.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.500
In other words, he made demons 
from his own flesh and blood.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.250
That's serious hax...

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.310
Hax?

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:49.900
It means he's a cheater.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:53.480
Also, only blades could harm him.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:56.670
Arrows and magic wouldn't 
even leave a mark...

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.410
and his weapon of choice was Overeater.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.180
He was a madman who'd roar with laughter

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:05.530
as he created armies by cutting down 
enemies and getting cut himself.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.730
Eventually, he came to 
be called the High King,

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.160
meaning the king of all kings.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:15.110
This city was once a vital 
hub for lake transportation,

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:18.150
but it only held out for a 
matter of days before it fell.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:23.170
The High King made his home in the 
city and mass-produced demons,

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:26.580
which used the water routes to 
attack surrounding settlements.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.480
No one could kill the High King.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.010
The destruction of the continent 
of Southmark was assured.

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:35.830
Just when everyone had begun 
to believe that, Gus...

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.160
Augustus, the Wandering Sage,

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.740
suggested that now was the perfect 
time to strike down the High King.

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:46.150
"Now"? Was it even possible to kill him?

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:51.250
<i>An army of demons, a demonblade, 
the city underground,</i>

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:55.840
<i>Blood's combat techniques,
Mary's blessing, Gus's tactics...</i>

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.080
Gus—

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.110
I get it.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.270
You do?

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.550
Really?

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:02.130
Yeah, I think so.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.990
Gus was hoping to pinpoint 
the enemy's location,

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.230
then invade via the underground 
with a few elite soldiers

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.380
and steal his demonblade in battle.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.980
It was probably the only way.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.190
The High King couldn't be killed.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:18.120
The premise was that he could 
heal using the demonblade,

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.410
but the demonblade is a 
weapon that can be stolen.

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:23.910
Stealing it would change everything.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:27.580
To do it, Gus would use great magic 
to wipe out all of his minions

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:29.030
and face him one-on-one.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:31.830
As long as Mary kept them both 
healed with her blessing,

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.640
no new demons would appear.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.190
From there, Blood would just do what 
it took to steal the demonblade.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:37.960
This was almost certainly successful.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.530
How can you be so sure?

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.880
The proof is that you own the demonblade.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.250
That's how the High King died... I guess.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.240
And after that—

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.550
Not quite, Will.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:51.260
You really are a genius,

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:53.480
but you've got the wrong conclusion there.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:59.130
We... I... didn't succeed in killing him.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:01.620
You... didn't succeed?

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.330
That's right.

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:06.700
Gus made use of every factor visible to him

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:09.610
to draw in any possibility 
of killing the High King.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.010
But...

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:15.230
The factors he could see 
were not all of them.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.640
The High King revealed his true nature,

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.840
taking on the appearance of a 
hideous, grotesque warrior.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.220
And then... well...

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.900
He was a better swordsman than me.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.250
I couldn't touch him.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.400
I'd fought opponents bigger than 
me many times before,

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:35.900
but he was the first one that 
nothing I did could reach.

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:38.370
Even you were no match for him?

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.470
Yeah, even as my buddies who 
were forming a wall outside

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:44.260
after entrusting everything to me 
were crushed one after another.

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:48.540
I had the support of Gus's 
magic and Mary's blessing,

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:50.500
and he was wounded.

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:55.740
Despite all that, I'm pretty sure 
he had made it one level higher...

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:58.690
enough to become something I 
couldn't kill so long as I lived.

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:03.410
To this day, I still wonder 
what I was lacking.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.520
But it's too late now.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.490
You know why, don't you?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.060
The undead don't grow.

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:13.970
My sword skills can't improve any further.

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:18.510
And when it became clear 
that we were bound to lose,

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:22.070
Gus and I placed a seal on the High King.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:24.700
If we couldn't kill him, 
we could, at least, do that.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:26.080
You mean...

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:30.210
<i>They gave up on Blood's chance of winning.</i>

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.970
Thankfully, the technique worked,

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.140
and the High King was sealed 
deep beneath this land.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:38.390
In other words...

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:43.510
In the very end, we couldn't 
fully believe in Blood.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.080
And then...

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.910
Mary?

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:51.760
And then an Echo of Stagnate descended.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.230
What?! An Echo is a body 
double of a god, right?

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:56.440
But why would...

00:16:56.780 --> 00:17:00.750
The evil gods act individually, 
each following their own principles.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.120
They will cooperate if it is in 
all parties' best interests,

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.870
but the opposite is also true.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.470
I guess Stagnate wasn't 
too happy with any of it.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:12.660
The High King was a monster that could 
slay a god's Echo using Overeater.

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:16.270
He thought it'd be better for him 
if the High King was sealed,

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.420
so he offered us a deal.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:20.590
"You three are exceptionally gifted,

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:24.030
so become undead and fight 
on my side," he said.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:25.190
But that's...

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.650
If we did that, he'd get rid 
of the demons in this city.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:33.190
After that, we could just watch over the 
seal as we pleased in our immortal bodies.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.950
Stagnate couldn't bear to watch 
the tragedies of life and death,

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.240
so he hoped to create an eternally 
stagnant world with no tragedies

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:44.690
by turning as many exceptional 
souls as he could into undead.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.220
And we had caught Stagnate's eye.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:51.500
Isn't it more accurate to 
say he set his eyes on us?

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:55.890
He told us to choose, but there 
was no choice for us to make.

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:01.320
We accepted his hand.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:05.230
Since my flesh was all cut 
up, I became a skeleton.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:09.530
Mary was burned by Mater's 
flames, becoming a mummy.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:12.490
And perhaps because he had no 
attachment to his aged body,

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:14.020
Gus became a ghost.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.520
<i>Mary did tell me once...</i>

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:22.040
That happens because I betrayed 
the earth-mother Mater.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.940
The god of the undead then 
cleared out the entire city.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.080
His overwhelming power turned the 
lower-ranking demons undead,

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.850
something that shouldn't even be possible.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:36.460
And the undead demons still 
roam the city to this day...

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:40.390
And we became the guardians 
of the High King's seal,

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.590
as the highest-ranking undead.

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:44.250
In the 200 years since then,

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:46.180
we buried our former allies,

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.880
and Gus set up a security net using magic,

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:51.780
allowing us to continue protecting the city.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:54.150
We didn't have anything else to do.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.200
We were bound to this city by our contract.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.750
We can't even find out what goes on outside.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:04.610
The three of us talked about the possibility 
that humanity had already died out.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.910
And then...

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.120
you came along.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:13.770
Or, more accurately, 
demons brought you here.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:14.920
Oh...

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:19.930
So I was meant to be a sacrifice 
to break the High King's seal.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.210
No wonder you couldn't tell me before.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.250
You couldn't bring yourselves to.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:29.300
Yes. As crude as he is, 
even Blood was careful about that.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.310
You really just called me crude, huh?

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.220
After the demons were defeated,

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:37.020
we argued with Gus a bit over 
what we should do with you.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:37.810
Argued?

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.110
Gus was against it,

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.470
but we decided to raise you.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.570
So that's why Gus said...

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:48.680
When you brought back a human child,

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:51.320
I thought you shouldn't have bothered...

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.160
The fact that the demons 
were able to bring you here

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:58.880
means there must be a place inhabited 
by humans relatively close by.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:02.960
The situation outside might 
be pretty gruesome right now,

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:06.980
but if it is, you just need to build 
the strength to bust through it.

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.260
Like you have.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.610
And that's why I'm here right now, huh?

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:17.220
<i>I'm about to head into a nation of people 
who survived the great uprising.</i>

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:20.250
<i>I'll take with me the strength 
that the three of them gave me.</i>

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:23.080
<i>One day, I'll come back to this city.</i>

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.100
<i>I'll bring my family and friends</i>

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.820
<i>and introduce them.</i>

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.620
<i>I could even rebuild this city.</i>

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.470
<i>One day... I know I'll...</i>

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.900
Be happy, Will.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:36.240
And don't forget to do good and pray.

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:36.920
Huh?

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.530
You were the best pupil 
I could've asked for.

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:42.920
Even in today's test, in terms 
of substance, you bested me.

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:45.670
You clever, precocious son of mine...

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.930
I love ya. Get stronger, okay?

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:53.330
In no time at all, we became a 
real family, and I was so happy.

00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:55.930
Will, my sweet boy...

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:59.520
Your mother loves you.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.960
Wait... Why are you...

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:06.210
talking like this is our last goodbye?

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:21.770
Have you said your farewells, heroes?

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:23.120
Yeah.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:25.950
Go ahead. We are ready.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:29.180
At last, you have lost your attachment.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.340
In accordance with our contract,

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:34.490
place your souls in my hands right now.

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:37.740
<i>I can't do anything... I can't move!</i>

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:38.840
<i>Why?!</i>

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.270
<i>Please, move!</i>

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:42.640
Vastare!

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.570
Devastate

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:53.900
Oh, yes. There was a magic 
user left among you.

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:57.960
Will, take Blood and Mary 
and get out of here!

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:01.710
Don't you worry.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:04.970
Episode 3
Payday

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:03.850
I will stop him!

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:39.970
Episode 4
The Goddess of the Divine Torch
